# A land played from the graveyard is still the turn's land play (CR 305.2): on turn three, after Bot1 plays a Mountain from its
# hand, the Marsh Flats in the graveyard cannot also be played (the refusal); on turn five, with the land play unused, it can (the
# positive control) and makes a Moloid. The Moloid's "you may mill a card" can be declined: attacking with it mills nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mole Man, Moloid Master
Marsh Flats
Mountain
Mountain
Swamp
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mole Man, Moloid Master.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot1.Search(Swamp)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
! Bot1.Graveyard.Marsh Flats.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Graveyard.Marsh Flats.Play
[T5 Bot1.Attackers]
Bot1.Attack(Moloid#1 > Bot2)
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 11
Bot2.Life = 19
